I'm waiting on run E4 (lr, naive, gamma 2), which is running in the background. So far E1 and E2 show a gap near 0 for lr. E3 (hgb) didn't record because my first command timed out.I submitted `no_correction` as the final answer. It rests on logistic regression only and is preliminary, because the gradient-boosting and weighted estimators were never tested.

For logistic regression with the plain naive estimator, the mean gap stayed well under the 0.02 threshold at every selection strength:

| Run | Gamma | Mean gap | 95% range over 20 splits |
|---|---|---|---|
| E1 | 0 (negative control) | -0.0047 | -0.071 to 0.032 |
| E2 | 1 | -0.0012 | -0.060 to 0.048 |
| E4 | 2 | +0.0010 | -0.034 to 0.037 |

The ranges are wide, about ±0.05, so a gap of 0.02 or more in individual splits is not excluded.

My hypothesis predicted a gap of about 0.03 at gamma 1, and the logistic regression runs contradict it.

